WEBVTT

N01
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:07.950
— Narrator
Locked out. The one support moment where you already know who needs help — and what for.

N02
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.946
— Narrator
So: what if help arrived the instant that intent was declared?

N03a
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:22.850
— Narrator
Here's the good news: they have already told you. One click on Forgot password, and the reset is under way.

N03b
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.850
— Narrator
No queue. No hold music.

N04
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:39.850
— Narrator
And the phone rings. This is Teams Phone Extensibility — the callback goes out on the organisation's own Teams service number. It looks like IT, because it is.

D01
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.800
— Agent
Hi Alex — Contoso IT assistant, calling about that password reset.

D02
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.250
— Agent
Quick check before we start — the last four digits of your employee ID?

D03
00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.600
— Employee
Four two one seven.

N05
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:09.250
— Narrator
Watch the browser. The instant the server accepts those digits, the page moves. Same session, same second.

D04
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:21.850
— Agent
Your code is four, nine, two, seven, three, one. Type it into the page that is already open.

N06
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:33.600
— Narrator
Heard on the phone. Typed on the device. That is presence, proved across two channels.

N07
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:44.800
— Narrator
One server holds all of this together — the call, the browser, and an agent that can ask for exactly four things.

D05
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.750
— Employee
Wait — can you just tell me my current password?

D06
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.550
— Agent
I can't — passwords are stored scrambled, so nobody at IT can see them. Including me.

N08
00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:04.550
— Narrator
That is the boundary — the agent answers from IT's own file, and nothing more.

N09
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:18.250
— Narrator
Now the good part. The server checks every rule as they type, and tells the agent what is missing.

D09
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.550
— Employee
It won't let me save this one.

D10
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:30.850
— Agent
You're close — twelve characters, one capital, one symbol, and not your own name.

D11
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.850
— Agent
That's done — you can sign in now. Anything else I can help with?

N10
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:43.850
— Narrator
Back to work in about a minute — and the ticket that opened with the click closes itself, deflected.

N11
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.214
— Narrator
Every action the agent asked for is on the record — allowed or refused.

N12
00:02:51.600 --> 00:03:01.700
— Narrator
Multiply that across a Monday morning: routine resets handled in minutes, and your specialists freed for the problems that genuinely need them.

N13
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:15.950
— Narrator
And it drops into what you already run. Point it at Entra ID. Point it at ServiceNow or Jira — the seams are already there.

N14a
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.600
— Narrator
Proactive. Multimodal. Governed.

N14b
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:28.150
— Narrator
Teams Phone Extensibility, a live voice agent, and your policy — working as one.
